NOTE - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

Musical notes for computer.beep. A note is a name
("A4", "C#5", "Bb3"), a MIDI number (69 = A4) or a
frequency in Hz (above 127).

note.midi(note) -> number

The MIDI number of a note.

note.freq(note) -> number

The frequency of a note in Hz: note.freq("A4") →
440.

note.name(note) -> string

The name of a note: note.name(60) → "C4".

note.play(note[, duration])

Plays a note for duration seconds (default 0.25).
Frequencies are limited to 20–2000 Hz.

  for _, n in ipairs({"C4", "E4", "G4", "C5"}) do note.play(n, 0.2) os.sleep(0.25) end
